\title{Refinement, contamination, and stop rules}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{refinement}
\tag{safety}

\p{Persistent refinement can retain useful procedures, but the same mechanism
can retain a specification exploit. A proposed change and committed
state have different consequences. Audit predicates can exclude specified
contamination, rollback can restore an earlier state, and resource admission
rules can prevent transitions that exceed the budget.}

